planet-ssh
----------

The planet-ssh module recognizes the following options: (See above
cisco-ios/cisco-cat section for descriptions.)

Option                  Description
----------------------  --------------------------------------------------------
user                    Mandatory. Used for the SSH authentication and, on
                        firmware that shows one, for the switch's own
                        "Username:" prompt that follows it. Firmware without
                        that dialog goes straight to the prompt; both are
                        handled.
pass                    Mandatory. Likewise.
enable                  Optional. Only needed if the account lands on the ">"
                        prompt: "enable" is then sent, and this is the password
                        given at its "Password:" prompt. Defaults to the login
                        password, which is what the observed device uses.
repository              Mandatory.
keep                    Mandatory.
timeout                 Optional, default 30 seconds (see the cisco-ios/
                        cisco-cat section).
banner_timeout          Optional.
type_delay              Optional. Milliseconds between characters typed to the
                        switch, default 100. Every line - credentials and
                        commands - is typed character by character with that
                        pause after each and three times that before the first
                        one: the observed device does not reliably accept a
                        burst of input right after a prompt (login fails
                        intermittently at full speed). Raise it if debug=on
                        shows dropped or garbled characters; 0 disables the
                        pauses.
fetch_timeout           Optional.
changes_only            Optional. The "! System Up Time:" header line of the
                        running-config changes on every run; it is kept in the
                        backup but ignored when comparing, so it alone never
                        counts as a change.
on_fetch_run            Optional.
on_fetch_cat            Optional.
timezone                Optional.
filename_append_suffix  Optional.
show_cmd                Optional. If specified, its value will replace the usual
                        "show running-config" command.
debug                   Optional. Boolean. If specified as debug=on (default
                        off), records to <repository>/<dev_id>.debug first the
                        ssh client's verbose account of the SSH authentication
                        ("Authenticated to ... using password", or why not) and
                        then the raw switch session (Net::Telnet dump_log). Note
                        the SSH login itself is not a switch dialog: "login as:"
                        is PuTTY's prompt, and the password goes through the SSH
                        protocol, so neither can appear as session bytes; the
                        ssh log lines are the record of it.

